Unfortunately ubms does not have any model averaging functionality built in. I may look into model-averaged prediction sometime in the future.

I would recommend either (1) fit one "global" model containing all the covariates relevant for your hypotheses/predictions (what are they?) then address those hypotheses in the results based on the parameter estimates and 95% CI. Or (2) fit a small handful of models, one corresponding to each specific hypothesis, then rank the models and interpret from there. If a few of these models have similar support, that uncertainty just becomes part of your discussion of the results.

Ken

